## File written
`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` (+140/−1). Nothing else touched — the other entries in `git status` belong to parallel workers, not me.

What it does now: for each corpus row whose top recommendation is in `COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS`, it spawns the front door (`execFileSync('node', [<root>/.skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs, '--hub', topId, '--prompt-stdin'], { cwd: workspaceRoot, input: prompt, timeout: 5000, stdio: ['pipe','pipe','ignore'] })`), treats any throw/timeout/unparsable output as no route, and calls `attachCommand(topId, route, row.prompt)`. Both new dist modules are imported via `pathToFileURL` after an `existsSync` guard in the existing `built … file missing:` style; a missing front door fails the capture instead of reporting a silent zero. `attachedMetrics` is appended after `rows`.

