## Note
My very first run of the harness exited 2 with `@spec-kit/system-skill-advisor dist is stale (source content differs from the attested build)`; a standalone `checkPackageFreshness` a second later reported `fresh`, and every run since is clean. The cause was a parallel worker's build (`lib/command-attach.ts`, `derive-command-bridges.cjs`, `MODE_COMMANDS` went from empty to populated) landing mid-run — which is also why attached counts are non-zero now. Nothing for me to fix; flagged so a later `dist is stale` on this harness is not read as my change.

Nothing I could not do: no build run, no `--write`, no git action.
